// tur_kit — the authored element-construction surface (the kit), a FILE
// MODULE TREE: this root declares the domain subtrees; every leaf under
// them is its own module (one class family per leaf). Consumers import
// through deep use paths (`use tur_kit::layout::flex::{ Column };`); the
// kit's own cross-file references are dot-qualified positions
// (`flags::MainAlign`, `handles::View`). Decls-only roots: no content
// lives in a namespace node.

// tur_kit — the authored element-construction surface (the kit).
//
// ONE wrapper class per element over its family's `tur` host-pkg rows:
// chainable methods (ONE METHOD PER PROP, named after the historical
// camelCase props in snake_case), `.child(c)` / `.children([...])`
// appending, and `.build()` as the ONLY terminal (each class's build calls
// its FAMILY's build row — `Column.build()` → `flex_build`, …).
//
// Construction law: build with the class call form — `Column()` /
// `SizedBox(400.0, 200.0)` — over each class's `[constructor] fn
// builder()` (the `.builder()` long form stays valid — byte-identical
// lowering), and CHAIN it: `let c = X().prop(..).child(..);` — never
// `let mut c` + `c.prop(..);` statement runs.
//
// Handler law: GESTURE handlers are MUTATIONS over the MutationCtx —
// `on_click(mutate(fn (ctx: MutationCtx, _e: nil) { ctx.set(x, v); }))`
// (the triad: source / derive / mutate, M1; A = nil is the click shape —
// one fn-type law for every payload). The kit seals the user fn into an
// opaque box and hands the ROW only the box; the flush's mutation pass
// invokes it through the dispatch entries (the dispatch module) with a fresh ctx
// (queued — never synchronously inside the gesture dispatch). The remaining
// fn-value callback props (on_tap / on_input / on_enter …) keep the
// sealing law — a named `fn` or anonymous literal, sealed into an opaque
// box, fired back through the dispatch entries — until the M2 sweep
// converts them to their typed events. The arity/type check happens at
// THIS boundary, at compile time. Nothing callable crosses the boundary
// as a string. `View` is the user-facing view newtype.
//
// Reactive law: every reactive-capable prop is ONE method over
// `Readable<T>` under the plain prop name (`text(r)`, `color(r)`,
// `width(r)`, `flex(r)`, `obscure(r)`, …). Static values wrap:
// `text(sv("hi"))`, `color(sv(0xFF..u64))` — the literal lane lowers
// through the existing static row via the handle's `get()`; reactive
// lanes bind atoms exactly as the old twin methods did. ATOM-ONLY lanes
// (`shadow_color`/`shadow_blur`/`shadow_dy`, `Table.rows`, the lazy
// counts, `Switch.value`) take NO sv — a static there trips the engine's
// loud atom-0 guard ("static value on an atom-only lane — bind a
// source/derive, not sv()"). A twin survives ONLY where an enum lane
// owns the plain name (`cursor`, `target_anchor`) — documented
// exceptions, not a regime. Sources /
// derives mint through
// `source<T>(v)` / `derive<T>(fn (ctx: DeriveCtx) -> T)`; ALL reads and
// writes flow through the ctxs (`DeriveCtx` get-only, `MutationCtx`
// get + set + run) — the handles carry NO public getter (there is no
// current store getter).
//
// Flag law: every flag family is a NAME-ONLY enum (`Align`, `MainAlign`,
// `CrossAlign`, `MainAxisSize`, `Clip`, `BorderPosition`, `Axis`,
// `BoxFit`, `StackFit`, `FlexFit`, `Cursor`, `HitTest`, `SpanFlags`) —
// no explicit int values. The private exhaustive `when` mappers (`code`)
// are the SOLE carriers of the row codes (verbatim from the Rust
// consts); kit methods take the enum and unwrap once at the row
// (`flex_main_align(self.spec, code(v))`). Cross-family misuse is a
// compile error. The `tur_host` u64 consts stay pushed for the phase-5
// test migration; the raw-const method overloads below are the same
// story.
//
// Color law: every `packed: u64` color prop (`color` /
// `placeholder_color` / `cursor_color` / `border` / `shadow` / `span_add`)
// packs **`0xRRGGBBAA`** — R in bits 31..24, A in bits 7..0. An OPAQUE
// color is `0xRRGGBBFF`; passing a bare `0xRRGGBB` shifts the channels
// (it decodes as a translucent `0x00'GG'BB'??` cyan-ish wash — the law is
// pinned natively by `tests/element/color_packing_law.rs`).
//
// The kit lives OUTSIDE core/ (the layering law): core owns mechanism,
// each plugin owns its spec + rows, and this module — registered as a
// compile-session prelude by the standard bundle assembly — is the stable
// authored surface rut modules import (`use tur_kit::handles::{ mount };`-style deep paths).
//
// Shape note: every class holds exactly ONE `spec: opaque` field (the
// family's host-side spec) — no rut-side containers; the host spec
// accumulates children through the `*_child` rows.

pub mod handles;
mod dispatch;
pub mod reactive;
pub mod flags;
pub mod layout;
pub mod text;
pub mod gesture;
pub mod control_flow;
pub mod scroll;
pub mod image;
pub mod virtual_app;
